@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam roundCorner 10

title EduCore — Lecturer Teaching & Assessment Workflows

actor "Lecturer" as Lecturer
participant "Vue 3 SPA\n(Inertia.js)" as UI
participant "Lecturer Controller\n& Section Policy" as Backend
database "PostgreSQL DB" as DB
storage "MinIO Storage" as MinIO

== Workspace & Schedule ==
Lecturer -> UI : Sign in
UI -> Backend : Authenticate session
Backend --> UI : Return role 'lecturer'
UI -> UI : Redirect to /dashboard
UI -> Backend : GET /dashboard
Backend -> DB : Fetch assigned sections & today's timetable slots
Backend --> UI : Display teaching dashboard & schedule

== Attendance Session Recording ==
Lecturer -> UI : Select Section & open Attendance
UI -> Backend : GET /attendance/sections/{id}
Backend --> UI : Return enrolled student roster
Lecturer -> UI : Mark status for students (Present / Absent / Late / Excused)
Lecturer -> UI : Click 'Save Attendance'
UI -> Backend : POST /attendance/sections/{id}
Backend -> DB : Upsert records in attendance_records
Backend --> UI : Confirm attendance recorded toast

== Material Upload & Assignment Publishing ==
Lecturer -> UI : Open Coursework & click 'Upload Material'
Lecturer -> UI : Attach syllabus/slides & submit
UI -> Backend : POST /coursework/sections/{id}/materials
Backend -> MinIO : Upload file to S3 bucket
Backend -> DB : Insert course_materials record
Backend --> UI : Material published

== Grade Calculation & Submission ==
Lecturer -> UI : Open /grades/sections/{id}
Lecturer -> UI : Enter Midterm, Final, & Coursework marks
Lecturer -> UI : Click 'Compute Final Grades'
UI -> Backend : POST /grades/sections/{id} (Compute)
Backend -> Backend : Calculate weighted totals & map to letter grades
Backend --> UI : Return computed grade summary table
Lecturer -> UI : Click 'Submit for Approval'
UI -> Backend : POST /grades/sections/{id}/submit
Backend -> DB : Update status to 'submitted' (locks lecturer editing)
Backend --> UI : Display 'Grades submitted for department review'

@enduml
